Nautilus.Integrate.gauss_legendre_5: n_points must be 5

`n_points` used to be read once into a discarded binding, so the rule was
always 5-point and a caller who passed 20 expecting a 20-point rule received
5-point accuracy with no diagnostic (nautilus#80). The argument now selects
the order, 5 is the only order this entry point implements, and an
unsupported order traps rather than quietly answering with a different rule.
`Nautilus.Integrate` has no variable-order Gauss-Legendre rule to fall back
on; that surface is nautilus#104.
